3. Mathematical Background

This section is the engine. It explains why every component was chosen and how the system behaves in the real world.

3.1 Cost Optimisation

Total system cost C is the sum of all parts:

C = C_{\text{hub}} + n_{\text{zb}} \cdot P_{\text{zb}} + n_s \cdot P_s + n_p \cdot P_p + n_e \cdot P_e

Two recommended budgets:

Path Hub Coordinator Lights (4‑pack) Sensors (1 temp + 2 door) Energy Plug Total
Premium Ease HA Green ($99) ZBT‑2 ($49) ThirdReality ZL4 ($30) $35 S60ZBTPF ($13.50) $226.49
Optimised (under $200) SONOFF iHost ($59) Sonoff ZBDongle‑E ($15) ThirdReality ZL4 ($30) $35 S60ZBTPF ($13.50) $152.49

3.2 Zigbee Link Budget & Indoor Range

For a fixed transmit power P_t = +20\text{ dBm} and receiver sensitivity S_r = -100\text{ dBm}:

L_{\max} = P_t - S_r = 120\text{ dB}

Using the ITU indoor path‑loss model (path loss exponent n = 3.0, fade margin X = 10\text{ dB}):

120 = 40 + 30\log_{10}(d) + 10 \quad\Rightarrow\quad d \approx 215\text{ m}

In a real home with walls, practical range is 15–30 m per hop. By placing at least one mains‑powered Zigbee router (a bulb) in every second room, the mesh guarantees full coverage.

Diagnostic rule: Healthy RSSI ≥ –70 dBm. If a device drops below –85 dBm, add another router.

3.3 Sensor Battery Life

A door sensor (CR1632, 225 mAh) drawing 30 µA average yields:

\text{Life} = \frac{225}{0.03} \approx 7500\text{ h} \approx 1\text{ year (minimum)}

In practice, the sensor transmits only on state changes, pushing life to 12–24 months.
A temperature sensor reporting every 3 minutes draws ~15 µA, giving 18–24 months on a CR2032.

3.4 Energy Monitoring

For the ESPHome‑flashed plug, instantaneous power:

P = V_{\text{rms}} \cdot I_{\text{rms}} \cdot \cos\phi

Energy accumulated by Riemann sum every 60 seconds:

E \approx \sum_i P_i \cdot \frac{1}{60}\text{ h}

A Home Assistant template sensor multiplies kWh by your electricity tariff (e.g. €0.30/kWh) to show daily cost.

3.5 Sunset Automation

The sun’s elevation \theta follows:

\sin\theta = \sin\delta\,\sin\phi + \cos\delta\,\cos\phi\,\cos h

Home Assistant recalculates every 10 minutes. For rock‑solid timing, trigger automations with a fixed offset (e.g. sun.set_offset: "-00:30:00") rather than the exact elevation crossing.

