11. Architectural Justification

· Local‑first: Latency < 100 ms, privacy absolute, offline reliability guaranteed.
· Zigbee over Z‑Wave: Zigbee silicon costs $0.50–1.00/unit vs. $2–4 for Z‑Wave; mesh is self‑healing and has no device limit.
· Zigbee over Wi‑Fi sensors: Wi‑Fi sensors draw 80–150 mA during transmission vs. 30 µA for Zigbee, making battery‑powered Wi‑Fi sensors impractical.
· Dual‑stick, not MultiPAN: Nabu Casa confirmed multiprotocol does not work reliably. Dedicated coordinators provide separate, stable networks.
· Entity‑based automations: Survive hardware replacement without rewriting anything.
· Firmware lock on 7.4.4.6: Prevents catastrophic network loss from the broken 7.5.1.0 build.
· Matter‑ready, not Matter‑rushed: The architecture supports Thread natively when you are ready, with zero disruption to your Zigbee mesh.

